sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2019-boundary-19> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The proposed scale-invariant scaling of cognition predicts that swarm organisms should fall prey to the same kinds of cognitive illusions and failures of rationality as vertebrate brains, which the author says has been observed in ants and slime molds.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Swarms should show the same cognitive illusions as vertebrate brains";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Computational Boundary of a \"Self\": Developmental Bioelectricity Drives Multicellularity and Scale-Free Cognition”, Frontiers in psychology (2019), doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688; section “The Agent’s Evolutionary Back-Story: Scaling of Information by Bioelectricity”. Scope: Swarm and collective organisms (ants, slime molds) compared with vertebrate brains"
}
